{
  "id": "site.st_mary",
  "name": "St Mary's cathedral (Dome church)",
  "name_1343": "Dom / Mariendom, cathedral of the Bishopric of Reval: Gothic enlargement under way",
  "confidence": "attested cathedral (consecrated 1240) and Gothic three-aisle enlargement from the 1330s; the April 1343 site state is a plausible composite",
  "sources": [
    "history/dossiers/religion/churches-and-religious-houses.md",
    "history/dossiers/architecture/toompea-castle-and-upper-town.md"
  ],
  "period_notes": [
    "Rule (maintainer 2026-10-07): features dated after 1343 are left out; where the 1343 state is unrecorded, a slightly simplified form of the later, documented church is used (plausible composite).",
    "Excluded as dated later: the west tower and its baroque helm (1779), the later chapels, the funeral hatchments and monuments, the box pews, the brass chandeliers, the pulpit (1686).",
    "Attested for 1343: the cathedral of the Bishopric of Reval with chapter and cathedral school; the rebuilding into a three-aisle Gothic basilica from the 1330s; the choir and vestry of the early-14th-century phase standing.",
    "Site state (plausible composite): the chancel with its polygonal apse and the vestry are finished and in use; the easternmost nave bay is complete (arcade, clerestory, vaults, roof) and closed to the west by a plank screen; westwards the walls and piers stand at falling heights with ragged tops, the arches of the second bay are turned on timber centering, and the west front is a low wall with a site gate. A treadwheel crane works in the nave; scaffolding, a masons' lodge, stone stacks, a lime pit and a detached timber belfry fill the yards.",
    "Unrecorded, simplified later form: white lime render outside with buttresses; inside white wash with grey stone arch edges and square piers; tracery windows with stained glass; stone-flag floor where finished, packed earth on the site.",
    "Unfinished walls show bare limestone rubble inside and out; render and lime wash follow once a bay is complete."
  ],
